  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "Both issues fixed; 533 tests pass.\n\n**1. Counterparty review mail now uses the signer-link format.** The \"Sent to counterparty\" email (the one behind the tracker's *With Counterparty*) only carried the secure link reference and OTP — nothing openable. Added `external_review_invite_body` in `app/services/notifications.py` alongside the existing `signing_invite_body`, producing the same shape: name, lead-in, `Review link: {APP_BASE_URL}/negotiation/external/{linkToken}`, secure link reference, one-time password, expiry. `_issue_external_link` in `app/services/lifecycle_negotiation.py` now builds its body from that helper. The URL path matches the route the frontend repo registers for the external review page.\n\n**2. Already-proceeded contracts no longer lose the Negotiation button.** The screen stores no \"already proceeded\" flag, so after a reload a Legal Reviewer on a contract already routed to negotiation was left with a disabled button and no way forward. In `app/services/lifecycle_clauses.py`:\n- `_build_analysis_response` now reports `proceedToNegotiationEnabled: true` when a negotiation routing already exists (a failed re-analysis still closes it — a retry clears that).\n- `proceed_to_negotiation` is idempotent: with a routing present it skips the missing-mandatory 409 (which the reviewer could not clear from that screen anyway) and returns the real `negotiationStatus` and `routedAt` instead of a fixed `\"Ready for Negotiation\"` / `null`.\n\nReading taken: the nine endpoints named in the shared contract already exist here with exactly those paths and field spellings, so I treated this as the two behavioural corrections described rather than a rebuild of the module. The button-rendering logic itself (showing the \"Go to Negotiation\" link off `proceedToNegotiationEnabled` after a reload) lives in the frontend repo and is left for that side.\n\nAdded two tests in `tests/test_lifecycle_negotiation.py` covering the mail body and the already-routed path.",
  "files_changed": [
    "app/services/lifecycle_clauses.py",
    "app/services/lifecycle_negotiation.py",
    "app/services/notifications.py",
    "tests/test_lifecycle_negotiation.py"
  ],
  "lines_changed": 109,
