    "notes": "All nine endpoints the frontend listed are implemented here. Three differences from the frontend's spelling: PUT clauses/{clauseId} and POST clauses/{clauseId}/reject both return the FULL ClauseResponse (all 14 fields), not just the 4 fields the frontend listed — 409 on stale expectedVersion and 409 on rejecting a mandatory clause both hold. analysisStatus values emitted are exactly 'Completed', 'Failed' (pending re-analysis failure) and 'Blocked' (unsupported file format, which also returns fileFormatSupported=false, empty clauses, metadata=null); libraryMatchStatus values emitted are 'Missing' and 'Standard' — the backend never emits 'Deviated' today. proceed-to-negotiation is idempotent: once routing exists it returns the live negotiationStatus/routedAt instead of 409, and proceedToNegotiationEnabled stays true after routing (it is false while any mandatory clause is Missing or while a re-analysis failure is pending). retry-extraction returns a full ClauseAnalysisResponse. ask-ai returns 403 for TENANT_ADMIN (askAiEnabled is false for that role). ExternalSubmitRequest accepts an extra optional clauseRedlines array ({clauseId, clauseText}) that the frontend does not send; omitting it still works."
